# Gate Test - BONANZA's SWITCHES, KEYS, GATES and DRAWBRIDGE test course (SPEC.md 128.41), built only by the
# BZGATE=1 knob (make BUILD=<tree> BZGATE=1 bonanzadisk).  NOT a shipped course: the knob adds it to BZ_COURSES
# and makes it the pathway's pad 0, so a new game rests on it (title, Play Game, Enter).  Not on the TOUR.
# A PLATE (rolled over) or a KEY (touched) opens its CHANNEL for the attempt: every gate of it opens and every
# bridge of it comes down.  Each channel is its GLYPH, black on white, on all of its elements.
#
# START is a plate at 2 units with a pad for each ball and two switch plates (RING, BOX).  From it:
#  - east, the RING GATE (wy 8 - 9): a corridor shut by two ring gates until the ring plate is rolled over;
#    a goal (exit 1) behind them;
#  - south, the KEY GATE (wx 9 - 10): a lane shut by two plus gates; the PLUS KEY waits in a nook beside it;
#    a goal behind them;
#  - south-east, the TIMED DRAWBRIDGE (wy 11 - 12): six cells over the void, down 128 steps in every 256 (2.3 s each way);
#    caught up, the ball falls; a goal across it;
#  - west, the BOX DRAWBRIDGE (wy 10 - 11): two cells up until the box plate is rolled over; a goal across it.
course GATE "Gate Test"
width  128
origin 320
ball   rubber

uses gate

floor rect 8 8 14 14 flat 2   # the start plate
pad rubber 9 9
pad steel 10 9
pad glass 11 9
start 10 11
prop plate 12 12 channel ring
prop plate 9 13 channel box

# THE RING GATE: the corridor east, its two gates, a goal behind them
floor rect 14 8 24 10 flat 2
prop gate 18 8 channel ring along x
prop gate 18 9 channel ring along x
goal tile 22 8 flat 2 exit 1

# THE KEY GATE: the lane south, its two gates; the key's nook beside it; a goal behind them
floor rect 9 14 11 24 flat 2
floor rect 11 15 13 17 flat 2
prop key 12 16 channel plus
prop gate 9 19 channel plus along y
prop gate 10 19 channel plus along y
goal tile 9 22 flat 2

# THE TIMED DRAWBRIDGE: six thin cells over the void, down 128 steps of every 256
floor rect 14 11 24 13 flat 2
float rect 16 11 19 13 thick 0.5
prop bridge 16 11 19 13 period 256 on 128
goal tile 22 12 flat 2

# THE BOX DRAWBRIDGE: two thin cells, up until the box plate is rolled over
floor rect 3 10 8 12 flat 2
float rect 6 10 7 12 thick 0.5
prop bridge 6 10 7 12 channel box
goal tile 4 11 flat 2

target 60
way 10 11
